    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_lead_in_sea_floor_sediment'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Mass concentration" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction "mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as "nitrogen" or a phrase such as "nox_expressed_as_nitrogen". Lead means lead in all chemical forms, commonly referred to as "total lead". "Sea floor sediment" is sediment deposited at the sea bed.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::KJWKRKJK'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KWEEWGY6/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KWEEWGY6/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KWEEWGY6/>;
    dc:modified '2024-01-18T09:01:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_liquid_water_content'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. The "soil content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including "content_of_soil_layer" are used.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::KWEEWGY6'^^xsd:string .
